In recent years, electrochemical water treatments have been studied for the purpose of alternative conventional processes such as chorine, ozone and ultraviolet using electrochemical reactions, especially which have been widely used in ship’s ballast water that is the issues in the world. Electrochemical water treatments are usually carried out for disinfection on the electrode surface by the direct and indirect oxidations. In other words, electrochemical technologies have been recently become important processes for the reactions by different electrode characteristics. In particular, DSA electrodes have been developed using catalytic coating such as Ru and Ir. Ru is well known to be a profitable catalytic coating due to low potential for chlorine and oxygen evolution, but it has been reported that Ru has less effective for easily oxidation by using electrolysis, and Ir has lower activity than Ru, but it is certainly known to be more useful in durability. Also, due to Ru and Ir have limitations for the precious metals, this study was hopefully developed electrodes with high efficiency and durability as to how to reduce the precious metals amount coated with Ta. &#xD;
In addition, it is very crucial to be stable operation in oxidant monitoring studies such as HOCl generated from electrochemical water treatment. This study was detected the oxidants through electrochemical methods related to less environmental second pollution and highly accurate processes in the various oxidant monitoring technologies. At this point, electrochemical methods with chronocoulometry have definitely studied the possibilities of sensor measured by working electrode of the oxidants such as Au and Pt. Au electrode is known to be less effects from DO, and used for the electrochemical sensor. Pt electrode is known to be electro catalytic coating generated from hydrogen and oxygen, which is reported that Pt electrode has more corrosion stable in comparison with Au electrode, so we have potentially observed which electrode is the more availability for electrochemical sensor. &#xD;
Therefore, this study was technically divided two chapters, and development of DSA electrodes for electrochemical water treatment such as RuO2, IrO2, also using electrode such as Au and Pt, we researched availability of sensor while measuring electrochemical methods for the oxidants from generation of water treatment.&#xD;
In chapter 1, we examined development of energy saving DSA electrodes for electrochemical water treatment. Having made RuO2 and IrO2 electrodes, we analyzed electrode surface using SEM, and measured by electrochemical impedance spectroscopy of electrode surface resistance. And we estimated oxygen evolution potential and charge through cyclic voltammetry test, also from the experiments of potentiodynamic polarization, it was obtained corrosion potential and corrosion current density. Also, we observed durability for Ru and Ir electrodes using accelerated life test of making a DSA electrode. According to the results of SEM of x%IrO2 electrode and x%RuO2 electrode contained with Ta, mud crack has been found more than 1㎛ on up to 50% Ir electrode surface, also found to be formed a cobble stone-shaped crystal affected by amorphous structure. In the case of x%RuO2 electrode, mud crack showed to be more than 1 ㎛ on up to 60% Ru electrode surface, and grain with 60% RuO2 electrode surface appeared to be approximately more than 7.7 ㎛2. In order to understand the electrochemical characteristics of DSA electrodes, it was carried out for electrochemical impedance spectroscopy which was investigated to be the lowest resistance as 1.890 Ω with 70%IrO2 and the more Ir amount was detected lower resistance. On the contrary, the more Ta amount was measured higher resistance. Also, Ru electrode coated with 60% RuO2 electrode was indicated the lowest surface resistance, and the more amount of Ta showed to be higher resistance which is similar to Ir electrode. From the results of cyclic voltammetry test, 70% IrO2 electrode and 80% IrO2 electrode were obtained 3.3196 mC, 3.2303 mC, respectively, and 60% RuO2 electrode and 70% RuO2 electrode were 6.3151 mC, 4.7021 mC, respectively, where Ru electrode was the more proper for electrochemical characteristics than Ir electrode. However, from potentiodynamic polarization, Ru electrode was found to be easier corrosion due to low corrosion potential than Ir electrode. In the accelerated life test of electrode, 60%RuO2 electrode showed approximately 48 hours of electrode life, but 70%IrO2 electrode showed approximately 432 hours of electrode life. So, based on the comparative results of electrochemical characteristics of Ir electrode and Ru electrode, Ru electrode was more beneficial for resistance, charge and oxygen evolution potential in energy saving while operating electrochemical water treatment, but IrO2 electrode would be more useful to be considered about durability.&#xD;
In chapter 2, for measurement of oxidants generated from electrochemical water treatment use for Au and Pt electrodes, it was apparently developed sensors through electrochemical methods, which is induced reductions for HOCl in water(HOCl + H+ + 2e ⇆ Cl- + H2O). At this time, it was noted for sensor availability of correlations of charge and HOCl concentrations. Au electrode of reduction peak for HOCl generated about 0.65 V(vs. Ag/AgCl). In the case of an agitation of 300 RPM at 20 ℃ of seawater temperatures, total residence chlorine and charge by salt concentration(as 0.5 psu, 10 psu, 20 psu and 30 psu) were analyzed r2=0.97698, 0.95653, 0.99718 and 0.97699, respectively. And in the case of an agitation of 300 RPM with 30 psu of constantly salt concentration total residence chlorine and charge at different temperatures(as 10 ℃, 15 ℃) were analyzed r2=0.99571, 0.98598. Pt electrode of reduction peak for HOCl generated about 0.75 V(vs. Ag/AgCl). At 20 ℃ of seawater temperature with an agitation of 300 RPM, total residence chlorine and charge by salt concentration(as 0.5 psu, 10 psu, 20 psu and 30 psu) were analyzed r2=0.94565, 0.96652, 0.96494 and 0.96776, respectively. And, in the case of an agitation of 300 RPM and 30 psu of constantly salt concentration, total residence chlorine and charge at different temperatures(as 10 ℃, 15 ℃) were analyzed  r2=0.98924, 0.97549, respectively. In oxidants detection of chronocoulometry using Au electrode and Pt electrodes, despite concentrations of total residence chlorine were constant, changes of salt concentrations and temperatures showed different charge. However, as salt concentrations and temperatures are affective factors for conductivity, based on the results of regression analysis on total residence chlorine charge for conductivity, Au electrode and Pt electrodes had very high correlations of r2=0.98470, r2=0.96729, respectively. More than 1.0 ppm of total residence chlorine with Au electrode had very high correlations of charge, but less than 1.0 ppm in low concentrations showed low correlations of r2=0.76685. However, Pt electrode was analyzed that total residence chlorine was more or less than 1.0 ppm had r2=96569, r2=0.96046, respectively. In addition to chronocoulometry analyzing time, Pt electrode was the more suitable for the respond velocity which Au and Pt electrodes were 22 seconds, 14 seconds, respectively.&#xD;
Thus, for measurement of the oxidants using electrochemical methods, Pt electrode is the more valuable than Au electrode.&#xD;
